WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.033
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:04.701
I'm hanging out
with Zoe Saldana!

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:05.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:08.601
Star of
"Avatar: The Way of Water."

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:13.033
All of your scenes
are filmed wearing mo-cap.

00:00:13.033 --> 00:00:14.367
-Yes.

00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:15.901
-Those are motion-capture --
Are they balls?

00:00:15.901 --> 00:00:18.767
What do we call them? Capsule?
-Yes, yes.

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:22.501
It's -- There are these
silver balls that are detected

00:00:22.501 --> 00:00:25.234
by all these cameras
that are installed in a set,

00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:27.200
which -- We call it the volume.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.701
So, these cameras are all --

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:31.100
And they have to be at
the same distance to each other.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.467
And these balls
that are in your onesie --

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:36.133
Because you are wearing
a little onesie, like a unitard.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:38.100
And all these balls
are on different parts --

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.667
-Over your head, too?
-Yeah, well, the helmet.

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:44.100
The helmet has these balls to
identify the head of your Na'vi.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.767
And then the balls on your --
Why are we calling it balls?

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:48.200
It feels really awkward
that I keep --

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.667
-I know.
That's why I was asking.

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:50.834
Mo-cap? What do you call them?

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:52.167
-It's a suit.
It's a mo-cap suit.

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:54.067
-James, you got to invent
a new thing instead of balls.

00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:56.234
Yeah. Okay, yeah.
So, you're wearing the suit.

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:57.334
-Yes.

00:00:57.334 --> 00:00:58.834
-And then everyone's
wearing the suits.

00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:01.267
And what are you do--
are you in the --

00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:02.901
What's the name
of the room called?

00:01:02.901 --> 00:01:04.167
-The volume.
-The volume.

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:05.601
So, we're in the volume, okay?

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:07.701
Say I was cast in this
and I'm with you.

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:10.868
We're both covered
in mo-cap...things.

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:14.400
And we're in the -- And then --
What do you see in front of you?

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.000
Are there -- Is there --

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.968
-Other people in onesies
full of balls.

00:01:18.968 --> 00:01:21.367
[ Laughter ]
-There you go.

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:23.100
-That's what you see in front
of you, but we'll have --

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.234
-Now, are you embarrassed?
-The first week.

00:01:25.234 --> 00:01:29.133
The first week, you are getting
over just how tight it is,

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:31.100
the wedgie
that you constantly have,

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.801
how funny everybody looks
in their unitard.

00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:35.634
-Because you have to act
on top of all this stuff.

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:39.000
-But then after
you get over that discomfort,

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.634
you've been prepping
for this world and this part

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:46.300
for so long that everything
that's in front of you

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:48.734
just disappears and
Pandora really comes to life.

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:51.767
So, it is, in a way,
like roundabout theater.

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:54.667
And it's like child-like play.
-Yeah.

00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:58.033
-You know,
and it's been, by far,

00:01:58.033 --> 00:02:00.200
the most special experience
of my life

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.968
in terms of my career
and also, like, as a person

00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:06.667
because it was the first time
that I was ever sort of

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:09.367
having conversations
around, like, climate change

00:02:09.367 --> 00:02:12.033
and the environment was by
being a part of "Avatar."

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:14.200
-Yeah, that was a big -- Yeah.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.334
And is that another big point

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:17.634
in this new movie,
"The Way of Water"?

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:19.267
-I think so.

00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:20.567
But what's special about it,

00:02:20.567 --> 00:02:23.434
at the center of all of this
that's going on,

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:27.934
you get to see a lot of things
that we have seen in our world

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:31.267
from, you know, history and
what we're experiencing today.

00:02:31.267 --> 00:02:33.567
But there's a family.

00:02:33.567 --> 00:02:35.501
There's a family
in the center of all of this.

00:02:35.501 --> 00:02:38.234
And they just want
to stay together.

00:02:38.234 --> 00:02:40.767
They want to survive.
They want to thrive.

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:41.968
They want to be together.

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:43.300
They want to raise
their children.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:44.901
-Yeah.
-And I feel like that's

00:02:44.901 --> 00:02:46.901
going to be
the biggest takeaway.

00:02:46.901 --> 00:02:48.467
-Yeah, because
everyone can relate to that.

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:49.634
That's what you want to do.

00:02:49.634 --> 00:02:51.734
I want to show a picture
of just you in the --

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:54.601
-Oh, that was the time I took
a bath with Kate Winslet

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:56.701
and Clifton and Sam.

00:02:56.701 --> 00:02:59.434
-Yeah, so,
how big is this bath of --

00:02:59.434 --> 00:03:01.300
Are these different balls?

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:04.834
-Those are different balls.

00:03:04.834 --> 00:03:07.367
There are all kinds of balls on
the set of "Avatar," by the way.

00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:10.701
-So, there's ones on your arms
and legs and stuff

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:12.200
so they know that it's you
and then --

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:15.300
-Well, these balls
were intended in the tank

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.000
so that when you put all these
balls on the surface --

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.667
I can't feel comfortable
saying the word "balls."

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:23.601
-Yeah.
-But then when we're shooting

00:03:23.601 --> 00:03:27.834
30 feet deep,
we have no reflections.

00:03:27.834 --> 00:03:29.901
It doesn't affect the lighting
or anything like that.

00:03:29.901 --> 00:03:31.367
-Oh, my gosh.

00:03:31.367 --> 00:03:33.000
-No, Jim is a scientist.
I'm telling you.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.200
He figures all these things out.
And his team.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.667
He has an amazing team.

00:03:36.667 --> 00:03:37.901
-So once you dive under this,

00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:40.100
it's like diving in water
and they can't see.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:41.300
-Yeah.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:42.801
-I mean, that right there,
I would freak out.

00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:45.100
James Cameron would fire me
in two seconds.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.667
[ Mumbling ]

00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:47.868
He's like,
"Alright. Just fire him.

00:03:47.868 --> 00:03:49.033
Just get him out of there."

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:50.501
Because you have to act
on top of that.

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:53.334
-Yes. You do have to perform.
And 30 feet deep.

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:54.534
But we did our training.

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:57.334
-Can we see the dots
on Zoe's face, as well?

00:03:57.334 --> 00:04:00.501
Like, can we zoom in?
-Yeah, you can see the dots.

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:02.868
But can you see how happy
we all are?

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:04.868
We look like we're
five years old, you guys.

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:06.734
Like, taking a bath together

00:04:06.734 --> 00:04:10.434
in James', you know, bathtub,
which is huge.

00:04:10.434 --> 00:04:14.133
-When you see the film,
do you go like,

00:04:14.133 --> 00:04:15.801
"Oh, my gosh. Like...

00:04:15.801 --> 00:04:18.000
I remember acting surprised
Or acting..."

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.334
-No.

00:04:19.334 --> 00:04:22.634
I feel like "Avatar" is so big
that even for my brain

00:04:22.634 --> 00:04:24.634
that I forget
that I was a part of it

00:04:24.634 --> 00:04:27.567
and I'm just taken into, like,
this immersive experience

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:29.534
of what the movie
is going to be.

00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:31.667
It's going to be just as special
as the first one.

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:34.567
You have to go see it.
Just take my word for it.

00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:35.801
It's so special.

00:04:35.801 --> 00:04:37.934
-Yeah, I cannot wait.
We have a clip.

00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:41.267
Here's Zoe Saldana in
"Avatar: The Way of Water."

00:04:41.267 --> 00:04:43.267
Take a look at this.

00:04:43.267 --> 00:04:46.200
-He's targeting our family.
-You cannot ask this!

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.334
The children,
everything they've ever known,

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:50.601
the forest, this is our home!

00:04:50.601 --> 00:04:54.634
-He had our children.
He had them under his knife.

00:04:54.634 --> 00:05:01.334
♪♪

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:05.334
-My father gave me this bow
as he lay dying,

00:05:05.334 --> 00:05:08.400
and he said,
"Protect the people."

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:11.400
[ Speaking Na'vi ]

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:13.601
-This will protect the people!

00:05:13.601 --> 00:05:16.767
Quaritch has Spider.
And that kid knows everything!

00:05:16.767 --> 00:05:19.300
-Zoe Saldana, everybody!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:21.400
"Avatar: The Way of Water"

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:24.534
is in theaters and IMAX
December 16th.

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:27.133
We'll be right back
with James Austin Johnson.

00:05:27.133 --> 00:05:28.467
Stick around, everybody.

